<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nagarakretagama</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1365</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Desawarnana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nagarakretagama, or Desawarnana, is an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-javanese">Old Javanese</a> poem written in 1365 by the court poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpu-prapanca">Mpu Prapanca</a> in praise of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayam-wuruk">Hayam Wuruk</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a>. It describes the court, royal tours and religious life, and lists nearly a hundred places across the archipelago claimed as Majapahit dependencies, making it a key source for 14th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nagarakretagama.jpg" alt="Nagarakretagama" width="320" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nagarakertagama.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
